    given-names: "Diógenes"

version: "1.0"

date-released: "2026-11-10"

abstract: >
  RVAT NLQ Interface is a Natural Language Query (NLQ) prototype that
  evaluates the use of locally hosted Large Language Models (LLM's) for
  translating natural-language questions into SQL queries against Rare
  Variant Association Toolkit (RVAT) databases. The project includes
  a production Shiny application, benchmark execution workflows,
  manual Exact Match (EM) and Execution Match (EX) evaluation, as well as 
  Valid Efficiency Score (VES), amongst other performance benchmarking, statistical analysis and reproducible
  research reporting.

keywords:
  - RVAT
  - Natural Language Query
  - NLQ
  - Large Language Model
  - LLM
  - SQL
  - Ollama
